  "scope": "Functional post-capability raw Transfer source order, all spend event loop, note callback/event ordering, ordinary late volume recheck, exact two verifiable marker writes, and derived enclosing delivery rejection/parent-and-queue preservation. Concrete callback SCT/Merkle behavior and native controls remain open. No runtime/negative-control credit, atomic evidence refresh or full Transfer certification. Capability mismatch precedes effects. Missing reshape source is checked even for empty inputs. Captured source-id observation is passed to all note callbacks; ordinary volume source is reacquired after note effects. A successful nullifier callback dispatches an exhaustive ordered spend-event loop before any note callback. Note failure retains its failing cache, omits that semantic note-created event and stops the suffix; internal SCT events and partial mutations remain callback behavior. Volume recheck success derives the exact two verifiable [1] writes and their frame, with explicit entry/day key separation. The actual late spent observation after successful reshape derives a raw error retaining earlier child effects, suppression of volume payload insertion, and enclosing delivery rejection with original parent/queue retained. Successful reshape remains an explicit observed upstream interface, not an unconditional runtime theorem. SCT/Merkle, codecs, collection/ownership and durability correspondence remain open. Preserved qualified 01 is not double-counted; failed 02 is zero credit.",
